{{also|o-|Appendix:Variations of "o"}}
==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*o(b)}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*h₃ebʰi}}.

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix|cat2=verbal prefixes|cat3=nominal prefixes}} {{qualifier|also {{m|ru|об-}} and {{m|ru|обо-}} before certain letters}}

# {{n-g|prefix added to adjectives or nouns to produce {{glossary|factitive}} verbs in conjunction with {{m|ru|-ить}}, i.e. verbs with the meaning of making (someone or something) the mentioned characteristic or property}}
#:* See {{m|ru|-ить}} for examples.
# {{n-g|prefix added to adjectives or nouns to produce {{glossary|fientive}} verbs in conjunction with {{m|ru|-ить}} + {{m|ru|-ся}} or with {{m|ru|-еть}}, i.e. verbs with the meaning of becoming or receiving the mentioned characteristic or property}}
#: {{m|ru|о-}} + {{m|ru|зо́лото||[[gold]]}} + {{m|ru|-и́ть}} + {{m|ru|-ся}} → {{m|ru|озолоти́ться||to [[receive]] gold; {{i|figuratively}} to [[get]] [[rich]]}}
#: {{m|ru|о-}} + {{m|ru|зелёный||[[green]]}} + {{m|ru|-ить}} + {{m|ru|-ся}} → {{m|ru|озелени́ться||to [[become]] green; to [[become]] [[plant]]ed}}
#: {{m|ru|о-}} + {{m|ru|безлю́дный||[[uninhabited]], [[depopulated]]}} + {{m|ru|-еть}} → {{m|ru|обезлю́деть||to [[become]] [[depopulated]]}}
